UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Treasure 018 - Maw of Nashal - ZTO' WHERE `ID` = 38498;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Strange New Ores', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain 10 Leystone Ore.', `QuestDescription` = 'You smell that, smith? Ahhhh... that there\'s the smell of opportunity.$b$bDalaran\'s taken us to some strange new shores, filled with mysterious metals. I\'m tethered to my shop here, but you... you\'ve got the freedom to explore and mine at will.$b$bBring me something interesting, and we\'ll see what we can make with it.' WHERE `ID` = 38499;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Leysmithing Mastery', `LogDescription` = 'Follow Alard Schmied\'s recipes in your Blacksmithing recipe list to build some Handcrafted Leystone Gauntlets.', `QuestDescription` = 'Well, now that we have the flux we can put it to work and see how it goes. Why don\'t you take a crack at it this time and make some gauntlets for me. I\'ll observe your work... from a distance.' WHERE `ID` = 38500;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Hatecoil Hammerwork', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain a Masterwork Hatecoil Breastplate and a pair of Masterwork Hatecoil Pauldrons.', `QuestDescription` = 'There may be a way to jump-start our research into leystone.$b$bI\'ve heard reports of naga camps down in Azsuna. If they\'ve been in Azsuna for long enough, their smiths have certainly started experimenting with leystone themselves.$b$bBe on the lookout for some leystone armor on the naga... ideally something more elaborate than a bracer.' WHERE `ID` = 38501;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Methods of the Nightfallen', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain an Ancient Sentry Construct Memory Core.', `QuestDescription` = 'I have a theory, $n.$b$bHave you encountered the nightfallen elves of Azsuna? They descend from the Highborne, and the accomplishments of Highborne smiths are legendary.$b$bThese fallen elves do a bit of arcane tinkering, crafting sentries to patrol their camps.$b$bBring me a memory core from one of their constructs. Who knows what manner of smithlore might lie within!' WHERE `ID` = 38502;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Treasure 020 - Helheim - ZTO' WHERE `ID` = 38503;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Shrine of the Bear Twins' WHERE `ID` = 38504;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Engineers: Not COMPLETELY Useless', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Ancient Sentry Construct Memory Core to Timofey Oshenko in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'Unfortunately, I have no idea how to access any information within this core. But I know someone who does.$b$bHead over to "Like Clockwork", the engineering shop three doors down from here. Timofey Oshenko owes me a favor. He should be able to extract the memory out of the core.' WHERE `ID` = 38505;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Chicken Scratch', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Ancient Highborne Data Printout to Professor Pallin in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'I think I have just the thing to extract the information from this core for you.$b$b<Timofey loads the core into the hopper of a clearly goblin-made machine, then covers his ears.>$b$bYou may wish to avert your eyes, blacksmith.' WHERE `ID` = 38506;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Secrets of Leysmithing', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Leysmithing Guide to Alard Schmied in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'I could spend hours poring over the details of this fascinating manuscript!$b$b...is what I would say if this weren\'t the simplest of tasks for someone of my skill level. It\'s about something called "Leysmithing". Here.$b$b<The gnome scribbles down a translation on the back of the scroll.>$b$bThere it is, word-for-word. Bring me something interesting next time.' WHERE `ID` = 38507;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Shrine of the Bear Twins - Reward' WHERE `ID` = 38508;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Treasure 021 - Helheim - ZTO' WHERE `ID` = 38509;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Treasure 021 - Helheim - ZTO' WHERE `ID` = 38510;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Treasure 022 - Helheim - ZTO' WHERE `ID` = 38511;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Oakleaf' WHERE `ID` = 38512;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Highmountain Smiths', `LogDescription` = 'Speak with Barm Stonebreaker in Highmountain.', `QuestDescription` = 'I think we\'ve gone as far as we can go with what I know, $n.$b$bThe tauren of Highmountain must have some smiths among their ranks. See if you can find out how to further progress our leysmithing abilities from them.' WHERE `ID` = 38513;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'You Are Not Worthy', `LogDescription` = 'Use your blacksmithing skill to craft a pair of Leystone Gauntlets for Barm.', `QuestDescription` = 'You wish me to teach you how to strengthen your crafts? We do not simply share the secrets of our trade with outsiders who ask for them.$b$bWe do, however, respect craftsmanship and discipline.$b$bLet\'s see your hammerwork. Our greenhorn trainees use those small anvils over there. Craft your best pair of gauntlets so I may judge your work.' WHERE `ID` = 38514;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Nature Provides', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain 10 Foxflower.$b$bIf you are not an herbalist, you can purchase Foxflower on the Auction House, or you can obtain it from another player.', `QuestDescription` = 'This is interesting, it says that leystone reacts violently with anything it views as a contaminant. Our foreign-mined flux was enough to cause the small explosion.$b$bLocal ingredients, however, have learned to coexist with leystone. Up in Highmountain, an herb called foxflower grows that can be turned into a suitable flux.$b$bGo and gather some foxflower that we can turn into a usable flux.' WHERE `ID` = 38515;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Treasure 022 - Helheim - ZTO' WHERE `ID` = 38516;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tayla\'s Rescue' WHERE `ID` = 38517;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'From One Master to Another', `LogDescription` = 'Go back to Alard in Dalaran and share what you\'ve learned from the Tauren.', `QuestDescription` = 'Now young one, go back to your master$bin Dalaran and continue to practice your swing. We\'ll always be here if you wish to come back and learn more.' WHERE `ID` = 38518;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Grayheft', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain Grayheft, Ancient Hammer of the Highmountain Tauren from Kubrul within the Deep Roads cavern.', `QuestDescription` = 'Our tribe regularly crafts legplates out of leystone. I will share our pattern with you... if you do me a favor.$b$bMy father fell to the drogbar several years ago, and they took his hammer as a trophy. That hammer was in my family for countless generations. Now, it languishes in the hands of the vile drogbar, Kubrul.$b$bI would very much like to have it back.' WHERE `ID` = 38519;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Heart of a Dragon' WHERE `ID` = 38520;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tayla\'s Rescue - Reward' WHERE `ID` = 38521;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Not Just Weapons and Armor', `LogDescription` = 'Craft 4 Hard Leystone Bars and 24 Hard Leystone Nails.', `QuestDescription` = 'You know, we aren\'t just limited to armorsmithing and weaponsmithing. I regularly make chisels for the scribes, crucibles for the alchemists, and even thimbles for the tailors.$b$bThey should sew in full plate gauntlets if they\'re really all that worried about their poor little thumbs.$b$bAnyhow, I have a recipe I think an adventurer like you might be interested in. Let\'s try it out.' WHERE `ID` = 38522;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Leystone Hoofplates', `LogDescription` = 'Approach Mei Francis in Dalaran while mounted to have your Leystone Hoofplates fitted.', `QuestDescription` = 'Here, bring these hoofplates to Mei Francis, down at the mounts and pets store, to get your mount properly shod.$b$bI\'ll share the pattern when you return.' WHERE `ID` = 38523;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Felsmith Nal\'ryssa', `LogDescription` = 'Report to Felsmith Nal\'ryssa in Suramar.', `QuestDescription` = 'Word has been circulating in smithing circles about a pair of Illidari blacksmiths that have been doing exciting work out on the demon-infested front lines of Suramar. I\'d follow up myself, but anything described as "demon-infested" is a little too exotic for my tastes.$b$bI just make the armor. I prefer not to wear it.$b$bYou, though... you could follow up on this tip. Be on the lookout for Nal\'ryssa. From what I hear, she\'s a hell of a smith.' WHERE `ID` = 38524;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Part of the Team', `LogDescription` = 'Slay $1oa demons within Felsoul Hold.', `QuestDescription` = 'You\'re a blacksmith?$b$b<The elf looks down at your hammer.>$b$bStill working in leystone, are you? I might be able to help you out.$b$bAlliances out here are hard-won. You\'ve got a pretty face, but that\'s no guarantee that you aren\'t working for the demons. I can\'t afford to trust you yet.$b$bDon\'t come back until you\'re caked in demon\'s blood. Then we\'ll talk smithing.' WHERE `ID` = 38525;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Smith Under Fire', `LogDescription` = 'Follow Felsmith Nal\'ryssa\'s instructions to craft Leystone Boots.', `QuestDescription` = 'You lack recipes for boots?$b$bWhat, were you trained by a tauren or something?$b$bHurry up, then. We probably have a few minutes before the demons attack again. Here\'s a pattern - show me your work.' WHERE `ID` = 38526;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Nal\'ryssa\'s Technique', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain 60 Leystone Ore and 60 Felslate.', `QuestDescription` = 'Listen, $c. We need smiths like you to carry on the traditions of the Illidari, should we fail in our crusade against the Legion. You are ready to learn.$b$bBring me materials. Lots of them. When you return, we will have much to discuss.' WHERE `ID` = 38527;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Leystone\'s Potential', `LogDescription` = 'Use Felsmith Nal\'ryssa\'s technique to craft a set of Masterwork Leystone Armguards.', `QuestDescription` = 'As I\'m sure you\'ve deduced, all of the leystone recipes you know can be improved.$b$bBy learning to harness leystone\'s true potential, you can reduce the amount of material you use and still yield an equivalent result. Here, I\'ll show you.$b$bWe\'ll start, as one does, with the humble bracer. This particular piece of armor benefits from the addition of brimstone runes. See for yourself.' WHERE `ID` = 38528;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Treasure 023 - Weeping Bluffs - ZTO' WHERE `ID` = 38529;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Firmament Stone', `LogDescription` = 'Speak with Barm Stonebreaker in Highmountain.', `QuestDescription` = 'When working with felslate and demonsteel, one must use special equipment. Specifically, an anvil hard enough to withstand the energy given off when felslate is hammered.$b$bUrael and I no longer possess such an anvil. But your friends, the Highmountain tauren, do.$b$bGain access to the Firmament Stone, their sacred anvil, and we can start working with demonsteel again.' WHERE `ID` = 38530;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Leystone Mastery', `LogDescription` = 'Speak with Thala Steeltotem to purchase a Leystone Armor Stand, then hang all eight pieces of Leystone Armor on it.', `QuestDescription` = 'Smiths that seek access to the Firmament Stone must first prove complete mastery over leystone.$b$bCraft an entire set of Leystone Armor, then submit it to me for inspection. Thala can provide you with an armor stand.' WHERE `ID` = 38531;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Maw of Souls: Hammered By The Storm', `LogDescription` = 'Go to the Maw of Souls and recover an Ancient Vrykul Hammer.', `QuestDescription` = 'Your hammer looks weak, and would probably break upon striking the Firmament Stone.$b$bThe vrykul master blacksmiths of old were known for the strength of their hammers. The only way to get our hands on such a hammer would be to go where vrykul go when they die. To the Maw of Souls.$b$bThe goddess that resides over that realm is named Helya. She hoards the trinkets they bring for her own desires.$b$bDefeat her and you may be able to acquire such a hammer.' WHERE `ID` = 38532;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tribal Knowledge', `LogDescription` = 'Report back to Felsmith Nal\'ryssa in Suramar.', `QuestDescription` = 'First, however, you\'ll need proper patterns for demonsteel armor. While access to the stone is earned through hard work and perseverance, access to our recipes is limited to the trusted members of our tribe.$b$bPerhaps you should seek another smith if you wish to discuss demonsteel patterns.' WHERE `ID` = 38533;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Demonsteel Armguards' WHERE `ID` = 38534;
