UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Drive Back the Tideskorn' WHERE `ID` = 39998;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Rockaway Coast Treasure' WHERE `ID` = 39999;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'A True Hunter', `LogDescription` = 'Prove you\'re a worthy hunter by hunting Bonebeak Hawks in Sunfrost Glade.', `QuestDescription` = 'I don\'t know why Hemet hunts with Razik. His contraptions are unreliable at best! \n\nA true hunter doesn\'t need gadgets to hunt. They rely on instinct, skill, and agility.\n\nSo tell me, $n, do you have the skills of a true hunter? Better yet, prove it.\n\nTake down some of the Bonebeak Hawks that circle the nearby meadow.' WHERE `ID` = 40000;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Knocking on Valor\'s Door', `LogDescription` = 'Find Vethir in the Felskorn Camp.', `QuestDescription` = 'The Halls of Valor is your destiny to claim, but it is already in the claiming. The God-King befouls its steps with demons and wickedness.\n\nYour dragon allies have come to Halls\' defense, but they need your aid. The vrykul have taken the leader of the storm dragons, the one you call Vethir.\n\nFree your dragon friend, champion, and wash the Felskorn from the Gates of Valor!' WHERE `ID` = 40001;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'A Familiar Fate', `LogDescription` = 'Collect the Jailer\'s Shard from Dravax and free Vethir from his prison.', `QuestDescription` = 'We had come to defend the Halls of Valor... I was taken from the sky...\n\nI cannot break free of my bindings. Find the jailer who made this cell...\n\nSet me free, friend...' WHERE `ID` = 40002;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Stem the Tide', `LogDescription` = 'Use the Stormforged Horn to destroy the three Felbound Portals in Gates of Valor.', `QuestDescription` = 'Skovald has profaned the Gates of Valor with his demonic allies. Among his forces his twisted mystics have conjured portals to ferry his fel allies from their blighted worlds. \n\nIf we wish to stem this tide, these portals must be destroyed. \n\nI will gather my allies. Take this horn and signal when you have found a portal, and we will strike from the skies!' WHERE `ID` = 40003;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Break the Spine', `LogDescription` = 'Defeat Garzareth, Karuas, Muorg and Ravathes in Gates of Valor.', `QuestDescription` = 'To lead his tainted forces,  the God-King has enlisted demons of great power to act as his lieutenants. If we wish to end his assault, we will need to take their leaders.\n\nThese demons are too powerful for most mortals to face, but with the power of Stormheim at your disposal, they will prove no match for you. \n\nTake them down, and shatter the spine of Skovald\'s offensive!' WHERE `ID` = 40004;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Stormheim\'s Salvation', `LogDescription` = 'Defeat God-King Skovald in the Gates of Valor.', `QuestDescription` = 'It would seem that the portals we destroyed down here were not the only ones. Demons still pour in from the top of the Gates of Valor\'s edifice, summoned by the God-King himself!\n\nI cannot face Skovald alone. Come, champion, let us take the battle to him and end this threat!\n\nFor Stormheim!' WHERE `ID` = 40005;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Sylvan Falls Treasure' WHERE `ID` = 40006;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Fields of An\'she Treasure' WHERE `ID` = 40007;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Only Way Out is Through', `LogDescription` = 'Escort Thalyssra to safety.', `QuestDescription` = 'I have much to tell you, but it is not safe to speak here. I cannot hold this barrier forever.\n\n<Thalyssra lifts a delicate flask to her lips. Her eyes shimmer as she takes a sip.>\n\nIf we push through, we may find shelter up ahead.' WHERE `ID` = 40008;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Arcane Thirst', `LogDescription` = 'Enter Shal\'Aran and find something to sate Thalyssra\'s thirst.', `QuestDescription` = 'My people have subsisted on the Nightwell for millennia. Ancient mana is our lifeblood - without it, we become... well, you saw them out there.\n\n<Thalyssra holds her flask aloft, gently shaking free the last precious drops.>\n\nI\'m afraid I have been rather reckless today. \n\nAlready, my senses are dulling. Without magic to feed upon, I will turn. \n\nPlease... find me something to feed upon... anything...' WHERE `ID` = 40009;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tapping the Leylines', `LogDescription` = 'Explore Anora Hollow and find the Ley Station there.', `QuestDescription` = 'The arcways were built to tap into the magical leylines beneath Suramar. As we learned to subsist on the Nightwell, the old facilities fell out of use.$B$BThis chamber is clearly receiving power from elsewhere.$B$BThere is only a trickle now, but if you can direct more leyline energy here it will help to sustain us.$B$BThe closest source is to the north, near Anora Hollow.' WHERE `ID` = 40010;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Oculeth\'s Workshop', `LogDescription` = 'Give the First Arcanist\'s Token to Chief Telemancer Oculeth.', `QuestDescription` = 'We need to make contact with Chief Telemancer Oculeth, the man who developed Suramar\'s teleportation network. \n\nOculeth had a workshop in old Suramar, from the age before the Sundering. He may be taking refuge there.\n\n<Thalyssra presses a small coin into your palm.>\n\nIf you find him, show him this. Hopefully you see him before he sees you...' WHERE `ID` = 40011;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'An Old Ally', `LogDescription` = 'Find Arcanist Kel\'danath\'s hideout in Ambervale.', `QuestDescription` = 'I was on my way to Ambervale in hopes of finding an old colleague.\n\nArcanist Kel\'danath was fascinated by the withered. He studied them for years hoping to calm their feral nature or even cure them.\n\nWhen one of his subjects escaped and ran amok in the royal gardens, Kel\'danath was ordered to cease his research and kill all withered in his possession. He refused, and was exiled.\n\nIf Kel\'danath lives, he is near withered. And withered are drawn to old settlements like Ambervale.' WHERE `ID` = 40012;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Aethril Sample', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Aethril Sample to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'This herb has clearly been absorbing magical energy from the land. Filaments of ley energy course from root to leaf.$b$bYour herbalism trainer in Dalaran will want to see this.' WHERE `ID` = 40013;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Spayed by the Spade', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain a Pristine Pistil and a Stainless Stamen.', `QuestDescription` = 'The stem, leaves, and petals are dazzling, to be certain... but look at the pollination filaments, here, and the reproductive organs in the center of the bloom. They contain more energy than the rest of the plant put together.$b$bI suspect that we can more responsibly and efficiently harvest aethril by focusing on these parts.$b$bStill, it looks like this bloom has been damaged. I need undamaged parts if I\'m to be sure.' WHERE `ID` = 40014;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Ragged Strips of Silk', `LogDescription` = 'Speak with Kuhuine Tenderstride about aethril and the withered.', `QuestDescription` = 'Finely made strips of clothing, torn, tattered, and dirty: telltale signs of the withered.$b$bThe feral, degenerate outcasts of nightborne society must also be harvesting the aethril... but why?' WHERE `ID` = 40015;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Desperation Breeds Ingenuity', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain $1oa Chewed Aethril Stems from Withered in Azsuna.', `QuestDescription` = 'I believe we may be able to use this clue to our advantage, $n.$b$bThe withered are notoriously thirsty for mana, and will stop at nothing to get it. Perhaps we can study how they use the aethril and use the results to improve our own harvesting methods.' WHERE `ID` = 40016;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'A Slip of the Hand', `LogDescription` = 'Speak with Kuhuine Tenderstride about the quick-reproducing property of aethril.', `QuestDescription` = 'As you harvest the aethril, your hand brushes the flower\'s pollinating organs against one another, creating a reaction.$b$bYou may have discovered a new herbalism technique. Your trainer in Dalaran would be a good person to discuss this with.' WHERE `ID` = 40017;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Dreamleaf Sample', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Dreamleaf Sample to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'The herb is brilliantly green, paper-thin, and somewhat sticky.$b$bYour herbalism trainer in Dalaran will want to see this.' WHERE `ID` = 40018;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'An Empathetic Herb', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain $1oa Healthy Dreamleaf and $2oa Blight-Infested Dreamleaf.', `QuestDescription` = 'Something is different about this dreamleaf, though. It is less than pure.$b$bI have a theory.$b$bThe wilds of Val\'sharah have been blighted by a nightmarish curse. Sensitive herbs like this may be susceptible to such a blight.$b$bI need more information before I can draw any conclusions. Find me some healthy samples and some blight-infested samples, and we can continue.' WHERE `ID` = 40019;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Twisted to Death', `LogDescription` = 'Find someone in Lorlathil to teach you about the blight\'s effects on herbs.', `QuestDescription` = 'The corruption has completely taken this herb.$b$bThis blight is a mysterious force whose complexities transcend the teachings of simple herbalism. An expert in such infestation will need to tell you what\'s really going on here.' WHERE `ID` = 40020;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'One Dead Plant is One Too Many', `LogDescription` = 'Slay $1oa satyrs within Val\'sharah.', `QuestDescription` = 'We must exact VENGEANCE for this. While I understand the importance of the balance between the Emerald Dream and the Nightmare, this time it\'s corruption has gone TOO FAR!$b$bSatyrs. I blame the satyrs for this. Make them pay! Make them pay, and Elune will reward you with her bounty!' WHERE `ID` = 40021;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Choked by Nightmare', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Blight-Choked Herb to Wildcrafter Osme in Val\'sharah.', `QuestDescription` = 'Another plant, killed by the blight. This one coiled so hard that it starved itself of sunlight.$b$bYou should bring it to Wildcrafter Osme in Lorlathil. He won\'t be happy.' WHERE `ID` = 40022;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Last Straw', `LogDescription` = 'Use Tur\'xoran\'s Summoning Stone to summon and slay Tur\'xoran.', `QuestDescription` = 'We cannot falter in our crusade against this corruption, $n.$b$bIt is our duty as heroes. As herbalists.$b$bAs hero-balists.$b$bSlaying simple satyrs will not do. We must attack their leaders. Bring this fallen herb to Shala\'nir, in the northeast. Find Tur\'xoran\'s summoning stone, and place this herb in front of it. Then... rip off his head.$b$bDo it for the plants.' WHERE `ID` = 40023;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Foxflower Sample', `LogDescription` = 'Obtain $1oa samples of Foxflower, then bring them to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'Something about this herb catches your eye... and your nose.$b$bYour herbalism trainer in Dalaran would certainly be interested in studying some samples of this piquant new flower.' WHERE `ID` = 40024;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Teeny Bite Marks', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Nibbled Foxflower Stem to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'This herb has been chewed by some of the local wildlife.$b$bWhat kind of animal would eat foxflower? A bear?$b$bPerhaps your trainer in Dalaran will know.' WHERE `ID` = 40025;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Chase the Culprit', `LogDescription` = 'Find out what creature has been eating Foxflower, then chase it and catch 12 Chewed Foxflower Bits.', `QuestDescription` = 'This is a powerful herb, $n. Creatures will occasionally snack on some simpler herbs, but usually they avoid plants of such potency.$b$bI\'m intrigued. What kind of animal would eat foxflower? A moose?$b$bYou should investigate further. Find out what creature has been snacking on foxflower, and then see if you can wrestle some of the flowers from its mouth, before it escapes.' WHERE `ID` = 40026;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Pied Picker', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Foxflower Scent Gland to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'As you finish gathering the foxflower, a particular part of the bloom catches your eye.$b$bOne of the leaves has a small protuberance, right where it meets the stem. Further investigation suggests that this is where the foxflower\'s unusual smell comes from.$b$bYour herbalism trainer would be interested in seeing this.' WHERE `ID` = 40028;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Fjarnskaggl Sample', `LogDescription` = 'Bring $1oa Fjarnskaggl to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'To one not trained in herbalism, this brambly bush might appear to be entirely useless. Your training, however, reveals this to be a very special plant indeed.$b$bYour herbalism trainer in Dalaran will want to see some more samples of this.' WHERE `ID` = 40029;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Ram\'s-Horn Trowel', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Ram\'s-Horn Trowel to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'The rune markings along the tool\'s grip suggest that it was left behind by a vrykul herbalist.$b$bApparently, the vrykul are also gathering this fjarnskaggl. Your trainer, Kuhuine, mentioned that she had read about this herb in the past.$b$bPerhaps she might be interested in seeing the tools that the vrykul use to harvest it.' WHERE `ID` = 40030;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Vrykul Herblore', `LogDescription` = 'Find three vrykul Herbology books in Stormheim.', `QuestDescription` = '<Kuhuine studies the trowel further.>$b$bThis is a standard digging tool. There is not much to be learned here, except...$b$b...this DOES suggest that the vrykul are still actively gathering this herb.$b$bThe vrykul likely know much more about this herb than we do. All we need to do is find out where their knowledge is stored.' WHERE `ID` = 40031;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Missing Page', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Runed Journal Page to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = '<The page appears to be ripped out of a larger book. It reads:>$b$b"...the Cairn of the Sea, a place long-known to be beloved by the gods.$b$bHe placed his offering of fjarnskaggl at the foot of the cairn, mouthed the words \'Herbs beget herbs\', and received the blessing he desired."$b$bThis may be related to the books you brought back to your herbalism trainer.' WHERE `ID` = 40032;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Fjarnskaggl', `LogDescription` = 'Bring 20 Fjarnskaggl to the Wind-Worn Cairn in Stormheim, then earn the Blessing of Fjarnskaggl.', `QuestDescription` = 'There! It seems that there was a vrykul herbalist, Torgus, who brought a gift of fjarnskaggl to a seaside cairn - presumably in Stormheim - and by doing so received a blessing from his ancestors.$b$b<Kuhuine shrugs.>$b$bIt\'s worth a shot, though without knowing what you\'re getting into, you may want to bring friends with you.' WHERE `ID` = 40033;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Starlight Rosedust', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Starlight Rosedust to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'Despite all your training, the rose disintegrated in your hand.$b$bYour herbalism trainer in Dalaran will want to see this.' WHERE `ID` = 40034;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Gentlest Touch', `LogDescription` = 'Attempt to harvest $1oa more Starlight Roses.', `QuestDescription` = 'Sadly, I don\'t have any special techniques that can help you here. You\'ll simply need to practice your methods. Get back out there, and focus on a gentle touch when dealing with starlight roses.' WHERE `ID` = 40035;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Jeweled Spade Handle', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Jeweled Spade Handle to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'An immaculately carved spade handle lies beside the rose. Apparently the spade was more beautiful than it was durable, as the blade has completely fallen off.$b$bYour herbalism trainer may be interested in seeing this.' WHERE `ID` = 40036;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Spade\'s Blade', `LogDescription` = 'Find the Broken Herbalist\'s Blade.', `QuestDescription` = 'Did you notice the script along the base of the handle, $n? It says "Herbalist Tharillon," in the writing of the nightborne.$b$bThe handle does little for us, but perhaps the blade of this spade will give us some information on how to harvest the starlight rose without failing quite so often.$b$bI would start my search for it in Suramar.' WHERE `ID` = 40037;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Insane Ramblings', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Scribbled Ramblings to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'Scribbled, angry phrases on a dirty scrap of vellum. One part catches your eye:$b$b     "thinks $gHE:SHE; knows how to gather herbs$b $n$N$b$N$N    steal my blade$b  slit $ghis:her; THROAT when I$b$b        just need$b      a bit more mana$b    maybe aethril, yes..."$b$bYour herbalism trainer may be interested in seeing this.' WHERE `ID` = 40038;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tharillon\'s Fall', `LogDescription` = 'Bring 20 piles of Starlight Rosedust to Azsuna, use them to taunt Herbalist Tharillon out of hiding, then search him for information about herbalism.', `QuestDescription` = 'He mentions your name... his blade... aethril...$b$bI\'d say that this is absolutely from Herbalist Tharillon, and by the look of it, he may have succumbed to the plight of the nightfallen. Furthermore, if he\'s looking for aethril, he\'s probably in Azsuna somewhere.$b$bTharillon is currently our only hope for learning more about starlight roses. Seek him out, but you may want to bring friends... he likely won\'t go without a fight.' WHERE `ID` = 40039;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Felwort Sample', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Felwort Sample to Kuhuine Tenderstride in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'This herb bubbles and seethes with a foul energy. It is smooth, dry, and cool, yet somehow quite painful to touch.$b$bYour herbalism trainer in Dalaran will want to see this.' WHERE `ID` = 40040;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Felwort Analysis', `LogDescription` = 'Collect Ryno Bloomfield\'s Analysis, Dani Earthtouch\'s Analysis, and Lohor\'s Analysis.', `QuestDescription` = 'I sent felwort samples to some of my fellow herbalists, but haven\'t heard back from them yet. Could you please follow up with them and collect their analyses.$b$bRyno Bloomfield is currently working in Un\'goro Crater.$b$bDani Earthtouch is researching Freya\'s influence in Sholazar Basin.$b$bFinally, Lohor has been working in the overgrown portion of Gorgrond.' WHERE `ID` = 40041;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Emerald Nightmare: Felwort Mastery', `LogDescription` = 'Travel to the Emerald Nightmare and cleanse Cenarius of his affliction. Bring back anything you discover to Kuhuine in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'I have a theory on how we can better harvest this felwort, $n. You see, sometimes in order to understand how something comes into being, you have to work backwards.$b$bI\'ve recently heard of the corruption of one of our greatest gods, Cenarius. I have no doubt the same corruption that lives in these herbs also resides within him now.$b$bIf you were able to cleanse that corruption, find a way to understand how it works and remove it, I think we can apply that to how we harvest these herbs.' WHERE `ID` = 40042;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Hunter of Heroes', `LogDescription` = 'Deal with Vigfus Bladewind\'s warband and claim his blades.', `QuestDescription` = 'Helya has made a mockery of my order by creating her own "helarjar", powerful undead tasked with hunting down heroic warriors and taking their souls before my val\'kyr can claim them. Among them is her personal champion, Vigfus Bladewind, who wields stolen blades I forged myself long ago.\n\nHe has returned to Tideskorn Harbor with a full cargo of stolen souls to take to Helheim. Go there, kill him and his helarjar, and make the swords yours.' WHERE `ID` = 40043;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Shadows in the Mists', `LogDescription` = 'Defeat Captain Sten, Sigrid, Kjell and Halvir in Helmouth Shallows.', `QuestDescription` = 'Many of the Kvaldir here in the bay are former denizens of this harbor, cursed by the sea-witch Helya to do her bidding for all time.\n\nThe ones you read about, they still walk the stagnant waters. They could be given respite, should a kind soul bring it to them at the tip of a blade.\n\nSo tell me, how kind is your soul?' WHERE `ID` = 40044;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Nature vs. Nurture', `LogDescription` = 'Talk to $1oa Swamprock Tadpoles.', `QuestDescription` = 'I appreciate murloc-kind far too much to tell you to go kill all the adults.\n\nWhat we should be doing is setting up the next generation to be more peaceful; Murky is the best representative for this. \n\nBring him to talk to the murloc tadpoles. He\'ll get them on our side.' WHERE `ID` = 40045;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Scavenging the Shallows', `LogDescription` = 'Search the Shipwreck Debris in Helmouth Shallows for Havi\'s clue.', `QuestDescription` = 'The kvaldir exist to spite Odyn, and it is here their spiteful work is done. They rob the souls of the living - the souls not yet judged - thus robbing Odyn of his champions.\n\nThey bring them here to transport to Helya, though the mists obscure any indications of how.\n\nYou seem to fare the mists well. Perhaps if you search the wreckage in the bay, the answer may present itself. You outsiders seem to have a knack for uncovering the most hidden of secrets.' WHERE `ID` = 40046;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'I\'ll Huff, I\'ll Puff...', `LogDescription` = 'Collect $1oa Pufferfish Eggs.', `QuestDescription` = 'Murky is my favorite little fella. However, in order to lead a change in the murloc population here, he needs some awesome abilities.\n\nThere are a lot of pufferfish around in the water, and I think that they could be a good resource for him. \n\nKill a few and collect their eggs for Murky.' WHERE `ID` = 40047;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Strings of the Puppet Masters', `LogDescription` = 'Acquire a Rune of Dominance from the demons at Legion Camp: Chaos.', `QuestDescription` = 'I understand you were just here to deliver the vellums, but we could use your skills as a $c. Our forces can only hold back the demon invasion, disallowing us to send anyone further into the enemy\'s camp.$b$bThe stronger of their forces stay in the back, commanding from a distance. They carry enchanted runes to keep control over the frontline demons.$b$bI would very much like to study one of these runes. Please retrieve one for me, so we may learn from it and use it against the Legion.' WHERE `ID` = 40048;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Slime Time', `LogDescription` = 'Feed Murky $1oa Bunches of Slimeweed by swimming through them.', `QuestDescription` = 'Murky\'s a growing boy, he needs to eat! What better than slimeweed for a young murloc?\n\nThere\'s plenty of it around in the water amongst the murlocs; swim through it and feed Murky!' WHERE `ID` = 40049;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Shipwreck Cove' WHERE `ID` = 40050;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Fel Secrets', `LogDescription` = 'Read the Tome of Fel Secrets to choose between the Havoc and Vengeance specializations.', `QuestDescription` = 'The demons made a grave error inscribing their secrets into this book. The fel energy emanating from it is potent.\n\nBut there\'s only enough to enact one of the rituals. After that, the book will be consumed.\n\nIt\'s up to you to choose which secrets we want to use against the Burning Legion.' WHERE `ID` = 40051;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Ancient Vrykul Mastered', `LogDescription` = 'Return the tablets and codex to Professor Pallin.', `QuestDescription` = 'Here are those tablets back, along with their deciphered writing. You can take this codex back to Pallin, too. I\'ll start getting my things ready for when he calls me back to Dalaran.$b$b<Nicholo sighs.>$b$bLearn from my example, $n. If I were you, I\'d break free from Pallin\'s "requests" as soon as you can.' WHERE `ID` = 40052;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Our New Allies', `LogDescription` = 'Report to Allari the Souleater in Azsuna.', `QuestDescription` = 'Student! Your fellow demon hunters in Azsuna have sent for you.$b$bI can certainly appreciate your time being spent fending off the Legion, but it doesn\'t excuse you from your studies.$b$bWhile you\'re down there, I\'d like you to come up with some new glyphs for your abilities.$b$bSurely my genius has worn off on you and you\'ll be able to create your own recipes based on what you learn.' WHERE `ID` = 40056;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Price of Power', `LogDescription` = 'Slay $1oa demons to help lessen the invasion.', `QuestDescription` = 'I see, you wish to augment your powers through script. I believe we can kill two birds with one stone then.$b$bI need help here reducing the demon threat. Perhaps some more engagement with our enemy will inspire you.' WHERE `ID` = 40057;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Defense Symbology', `LogDescription` = 'Find Baric Stormrunner near the Ley-Ruins of Zarkhenar.', `QuestDescription` = 'As you know, $n, we demon hunters must keep our darkness at bay, lest we succumb to it and become demons ourselves.$b$bUp to the north, a demon hunter by the name of Baric Stormrunner is preparing to strengthen his markings. He could use your assistance with his ritual.' WHERE `ID` = 40058;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Opposites Repel', `LogDescription` = 'Collect ley dust from the nightfallen in Zarkhenar.', `QuestDescription` = 'The ruins nearby have had an eruption of ley energies. Twisted night elves deemed "Nightfallen" are scavenging the area as we speak.$b$bCollect ley dust for me from the nightfallen in the ruins up ahead. The dust is infused with arcane energy that I\'ll need to complete my ritual.' WHERE `ID` = 40059;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Containing the Demon Within', `LogDescription` = 'Assist Baric in completing the ritual.', `QuestDescription` = 'Now that we have all the essential pieces, let\'s begin the ritual.$b$bI\'ll instruct you on how to help me throughout it. It is pivotal that you follow my instructions when I give them, or the ritual will fail.' WHERE `ID` = 40060;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'To Know Your Enemy', `LogDescription` = 'Find Zaria Shadowheart near the Felblaze Ingress.', `QuestDescription` = 'As we fight the demons, we\'ve also been studying them.$b$bGreat understanding can come from gathering intel. I have a demon hunter near the Felblaze Ingress now gathering intel on the demons there.$b$bGo to her and see what she has learned from the demons invading that region.' WHERE `ID` = 40061;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Bulging Nightmare Pod', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Bulging Nightmare Pod to Professor Pallin in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = '<The flower has folded inward, to protect itself from the nightmare energy trapped within.>$b$b<Professor Pallin would be interested in seeing this.>' WHERE `ID` = 40062;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Control is Key', `LogDescription` = 'Destroy the crystal providing protecting Overseer Felorax, then slay him.', `QuestDescription` = 'I trust you remember why you removed your eyes?$b$bEven though we can see more clearly now, the demons have found ways to mask even their fel energies from us.$b$bA demon commander walks amongst the troops below, commanding them from the shadows. His cloak is powered by an energetic crystal.$b$bFind and destroy that crystal, then kill the commander.' WHERE `ID` = 40063;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Woody Seed Cluster', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Woody Seed Cluster to Professor Pallin in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = '<Attempting to mill this flower has proven more difficult than usual. Located in the bushy center of the bloom is a densely-packed cluster of seeds.>$b$b<Professor Pallin would be interested in seeing this.>' WHERE `ID` = 40064;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Fjarnsk', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Fjarnsk to Professor Pallin in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = '<A goopy substance seeps from the interior of the bloom. It\'s not ink... it is something else entirely.>$b$b<Professor Pallin would be interested in seeing this.>' WHERE `ID` = 40065;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Treasure 032 - Blackbeak Overlook - twh' WHERE `ID` = 40066;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Vignette: Boulderfall - twh' WHERE `ID` = 40067;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.0 Stormheim - Vignette: Egyl the Enduring - twh' WHERE `ID` = 40068;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Fledgling Worm Guts', `LogDescription` = 'Collect Worm Guts from Fledgling Rockcrawlers within Rockcrawler Chasm.', `QuestDescription` = 'The drogbar use these caves as a place to train fledgling worms.\n\nThe rockcrawlers are young and fairly weak, for now, but in time they will grow in size and strength. Without our intervention, the worms will morph into the monstrosities that the drogbar ride into battle.\n\nTheir guts are also known to be quite useful, and I have need of them. Two worms, one stone.' WHERE `ID` = 40069;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Eagle Egg Recovery', `LogDescription` = 'Head into Rockcrawler Chasm and recover eagle eggs.', `QuestDescription` = 'Eagles are revered by the Skyhorn tribe, but their numbers are dwindling.\n\nThe drogbar feed their fledgling worms eagle eggs so they\'ll grow strong enough to ride into battle. \n\nIf the drogbar continue to pilfer these eggs, the eagles may become extinct.\n\nHead deeper into the cave and recover any eagle eggs you can find.' WHERE `ID` = 40070;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tamer Takedown', `LogDescription` = 'Kill Tamer Korgrul within Rockcrawler Chasm.', `QuestDescription` = 'The drogbar will continue to breed vicious worms as long as their tamer lives. \n\nKorgrul is responsible for turning fledgling rockcrawlers into the monstrous siege worms that are ridden into battle.\n\nHead deep into the chasm and end his life, so that we may also see the end of these unnatural creatures.', `PortraitGiverName` = 'Tamer Korgrul' WHERE `ID` = 40071;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Halls of Valor: Securing the Aegis', `LogDescription` = 'Defeat God-King Skovald in the Halls of Valor and claim the Aegis of Aggramar.', `QuestDescription` = 'The Felskorn may be broken, but the head of the beast yet lives. The God-King will still vie for the Aegis if left unchecked.\n\nYou, who have completed trials upon trials, must not let this come to pass. You must claim the Aegis over Skovald\'s broken bones!\n\nThe Halls of Valor await!' WHERE `ID` = 40072;
