UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Secured Surroundings', `LogDescription` = 'Meet Nighthuntress Syrenne at Deliverance Point.', `QuestDescription` = 'With Lexera defeated, her band of trappers will quickly disband. Those that refuse will meet my blade.\n\nThese shores will be free of those who wish to corrupt Azeroth\'s wildlife.\n\nOur work here is done for now. Let us meet at Deliverance Point. There is more I wish to discuss in secured surroundings.' WHERE `ID` = 46235;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Stonebound Soldiers' WHERE `ID` = 46236;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Bloodbringer\'s Missive', `LogDescription` = 'Speak with Mor\'zul Bloodbringer in Dreadscar Rift.', `QuestDescription` = 'Warlock! We have news from Dreadscar Rift. \n\nA message arrived by raven from Mor\'zul Bloodbringer, with instructions that you meet him in Dreadscar Rift immediately!' WHERE `ID` = 46237;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'If You Build It', `LogDescription` = 'Collect 5 Felslate, 3 Chaotic Spinel and an Unbending Potion. These can be gathered and crafted using profession skills or purchased on the Auction House.', `QuestDescription` = 'If we wish to achieve a sustained connection to Xoroth, we\'ll need a particularly resilient portal. Unfortunately, we can\'t just summon this one up from the ground.\n\nI will need you to gather the requisite materials. Once we have them, I will have the mo\'arg begin construction at once. \n\nHere\'s the list of what you\'ll need.' WHERE `ID` = 46238;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Fel to the Core', `LogDescription` = 'Collect an Overcharged Fel Core from the commander of a Legion Assault on the Broken Isles.', `QuestDescription` = 'While it has become relatively easy for a warlock to open a brief window into the realms of the Legion, a sustained portal requires significantly more power.\n\nFor this, we will need a power source brimming with fel energy. \n\nI know that the commanders of the Legion use powerful fel cores to control their warships. If you can defeat the commander of one of these ships, you should be able to take their core.' WHERE `ID` = 46239;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Give Me Fuel, Give Me Fire', `LogDescription` = 'Collect 50 Owlbeast Blood from Owlbeasts within Lostlight Grotto in Val\'sharah.', `QuestDescription` = 'A powerful core will not alone be able to power the portal. Like any powerful engine, it will require fuel - though an engine of fel energy must burn life force to thrive.\n\nWe will need blood potent in magical energy to keep our fel core running and sustain our connection to Xoroth. Fortunately, I have experience in these matters, and I know just the place where we can get some.\n\nYou\'ll need a jar or something.' WHERE `ID` = 46240;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Minions of Hel\'nurath', `LogDescription` = 'Use your Succubus\' Seduction to question Xorothian Cultists within the Dark Stockades in the Broken Shore.', `QuestDescription` = 'The dreadlord Hel\'nurath gifts his lieutenants with calling stones to call and bind the dreadsteeds of Xoroth to their service. I believe one such stone will help us draw out the Wrathsteed. \n\nSome Xorothian cultists have been spotted helping the Legion\'s efforts on the Broken Shore. It would be safe to assume their leader has one of Hel\'nurath\'s stones.\n\nYour succubus should be able to entice the truth out of the cultists. Find one who knows of their leader\'s whereabouts.' WHERE `ID` = 46241;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Dreadlord\'s Calling', `LogDescription` = 'Collect a Xorothian Calling Stone from Zuriwa the Hexxer within the Dark Stockades in the Broken Shore.', `QuestDescription` = 'According to the cultist, the leader you seek should be in her tower overseeing the operations in the Dark Stockades.' WHERE `ID` = 46242;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Wrathsteed of Xoroth', `LogDescription` = 'Complete the ritual on the Summoning Platform in Dreadscar Rift to enslave the Wrathsteed.', `QuestDescription` = 'The time has come and the preparations have been made. When you are ready, we will tear a hole into Xoroth, and force the Arax\'ath and the Wrathsteed out of hiding.\n\nFollow me to the summoning platform. From there we will initiate the ritual.\n\nPrepare yourself, $n. This will not be an easy undertaking.' WHERE `ID` = 46243;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Altar of the Aegis', `LogDescription` = 'Defeat Lord Mephistroth and place the Aegis of Aggramar upon the Altar of Eternal Night.', `QuestDescription` = 'Champion, we are ready to assault the Tomb of Sargeras.\n\nI studied the writings of Aegwynn, the Guardian who defeated the Dark Titan\'s avatar. She said that if her wards were compromised, a failsafe could be triggered by placing the Aegis of Aggramar upon an altar in the Cathedral of Eternal Night.\n\nYou are the hero who acquired the Pillars of Creation, $n. Gather your allies and enter the Cathedral. Be warned: Mephistroth will use all his power to stop you from placing the Aegis. You must prevail!' WHERE `ID` = 46244;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Begin Construction', `LogDescription` = 'Use the Construction Table to donate Legionfall War Supplies to the construction of the Mage Tower, Nether Disruptor, or Command Center.', `QuestDescription` = 'We\'ve got the supplies. Now someone needs to decide what to do with \'em.\n\nHmm. Looks like it\'s your call, being the $ct and all!\n\nTime to pick a building to focus on.' WHERE `ID` = 46245;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Strike Them Down', `LogDescription` = 'Slay 100 demons on the Broken Shore.', `QuestDescription` = 'The Felstorm continues to rain demon scum upon these shores. Kil\'jaeden believes his army infinite, his resources inexhaustible.\n\nWe will show him how wrong he is.\n\nCut a swath of retribution through their ranks, $ct. Strike down demon after demon, until your weapons are bathed in their blood. And when they cry out for mercy, send them screaming back into the Nether.' WHERE `ID` = 46246;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Defending Broken Isles', `LogDescription` = 'Defeat a Legion Assault in the Broken Isles.', `QuestDescription` = 'In our zeal to reclaim the Broken Shore from the Legion, we cannot allow the rest of this land to fall into the demons\' foul grip.\n\nKil\'jaeden has dispatched his forces across the Broken Isles, threatening the homelands of the allies you have made. You must answer their call in this hour of need.\n\nTurn back these demon assaults with haste, $ct. The Armies of Legionfall will see that the Broken Shore remains secured.' WHERE `ID` = 46247;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Self-Fulfilling Prophecy', `LogDescription` = 'Complete 8 World Quests on the Broken Shore.', `QuestDescription` = 'In my life, I have witnessed many visions. Some filled me with hope... others, with despair.\n\nVictory over Kil\'jaeden lies within our grasp. I have foreseen it. But visions only show us where our path might lead. They require effort to become reality.\n\nThat effort falls upon your shoulders, $n. You have done much, but more is needed. Fight on the battlefields of the Broken Shore and forge a destiny free from the Legion\'s grasp!' WHERE `ID` = 46248;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Championing Our Cause', `LogDescription` = 'Successfully complete a Legionfall mission at your Class Order Hall.', `QuestDescription` = 'Important work has been done by your order, $ct. Your champions have succeeded time and again in undermining the Legion\'s invasion.\n\nAs we make preparations for our assault on the Tomb of Sargeras, we need to keep the demons off balance. By pressuring them at every turn, we will expose vulnerabilities that can be exploited to our advantage.\n\nSend out your order\'s champions, $n. Their missions are vital to the success of our campaign... especially as our confrontation with Kil\'jaeden draws closer.' WHERE `ID` = 46249;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Take Out the Head...', `LogDescription` = 'Slay Rare Elite Demon Commanders on the Broken Shore.', `QuestDescription` = 'The Broken Shore swims with Legion filth, each demon deserving of a swift and merciless end.\n\nBut some are more insidious than the rest. Powerful combatants rallying others to their perfidious cause.\n\nStrike down these demon champions and you will fill the hearts of their kin with fear and doubt. Break the Legion\'s spirit and we will break its back.' WHERE `ID` = 46250;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Shard Times', `LogDescription` = 'Collect $1oa Nethershards on the Broken Shore.', `QuestDescription` = 'As you have surely noticed, a slain demon leaves behind Nethershards, solidified residual energy from the Twisting Nether. I require a significant quantity of them for an experiment I\'m conducting... $1oa shards, to be precise.$b$bWhy are you looking at me like that? We\'ve had this conversation before. I did the math.$b$bI need exactly $1oa shards. Fewer would be inadequate. More would be absurd.$b$bDon\'t question my methods. Go!' WHERE `ID` = 46251;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Intolerable Infestation', `LogDescription` = 'Slay 50 demons in Faronaar or Felsoul Hold.', `QuestDescription` = 'While we purge Legion filth from the Broken Shore, the fiends maintain their hold on nearby lands. Their presence can no longer be tolerated.\n\nThe fetid strongholds of Faronaar and Felsoul Hold infest Azsuna and Suramar. Choose an attack point and cut a swath through their insidious ranks.\n\nReturn to me with demon blood on your hands, then we can resume our campaign to drive Kil\'jaeden from the Tomb.' WHERE `ID` = 46252;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Pillars of Creation', `LogDescription` = 'Use the Pillars of Creation to seal the Tomb of Sargeras.', `QuestDescription` = 'Our campaign on the Broken Shore has reached a turning point. The Armies of Legionfall stand ready to breach the Tomb of Sargeras and seal the Legion\'s gateway to our world.\n\nThe time to strike is now, $n.\n\nThe Aegis of Aggramar has been secured in the Cathedral. The echo of Magna Aegwynn said that the other Pillars of Creation are needed to seal the tomb. It is fitting that you have the honor of locking those ancient relics in place and closing down the Felstorm once and for all.' WHERE `ID` = 46253;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'TBD' WHERE `ID` = 46254;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'X Unstable Portals Disrupted, 1 World Boss Defeated' WHERE `ID` = 46255;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'X Treasures Found, 1 Challenge Attempted' WHERE `ID` = 46256;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'REUSE ME' WHERE `ID` = 46257;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Calm After the Storm', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the Doomstone to Neptulon in the Maelstrom.', `QuestDescription` = 'You have saved the elements from the Legion\'s control, and for that we thank you. However, it came at a great cost to both your health and your fellow shaman. Many came back to us wounded, dragged along by their fellow shaman.$b$bWe have seen the havoc the Doomstone can wreak. It does not belong in the hands of any being, mortal or otherwise. While you were asleep, the elemental lords and I discussed its fate.$b$bBring it to Neptulon. He will explain.' WHERE `ID` = 46258;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Darkbinder Dilemma', `LogDescription` = 'Kill Darkbinder Elissath.', `QuestDescription` = 'Ah, Delas sent you. I see.$B$BIt\'s good she didn\'t come herself. It would break her heart to see what is happening to our family.$B$BA demon is defiling our dead in the ruins nearby. She\'s using her fel magic on our ancestors, turning them into mindless horrors that do the bidding of the Burning Legion.$B$BI can\'t deal with the harpies and this demon, but maybe you could help?$B$BGet rid of the darkbinder that torments our dead, and I will grant you access to whatever\'s left of the Moonfang family relics.', `PortraitGiverName` = 'Darkbinder Elissath' WHERE `ID` = 46259;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Meld Into the Shadows', `LogDescription` = 'Return to the Hall of Shadows, and meet Lord Jorach Ravenholdt.', `QuestDescription` = 'We should meet back up with the rest of the council and tell them of what we have achieved this day. At your leisure, return to us. We shall be waiting.' WHERE `ID` = 46260;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Taste of Corruption' WHERE `ID` = 46261;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Save the Tadpoles!' WHERE `ID` = 46262;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Weaving Fel Webs' WHERE `ID` = 46263;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Their Eyes Are Upon Us' WHERE `ID` = 46264;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Fel and the Fawns' WHERE `ID` = 46265;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Return of the Slayer', `LogDescription` = 'Return to Kor\'vas aboard the Fel Hammer.', `QuestDescription` = 'If you\'re anything like me, I\'m sure you\'d prefer to remain here on solid ground.\n\nUnfortunately, it is probably best to return to the Fel Hammer right away so Kor\'vass can finish the repairss.' WHERE `ID` = 46266;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Return of the Battlelord', `LogDescription` = 'Talk to Odyn in Skyhold.', `QuestDescription` = 'Battlelord $n, Odyn will want to hear the tale of your glorious victories here!\n\nI will assist you in returning to Skyhold when you are ready.' WHERE `ID` = 46267;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'A Found Memento', `LogDescription` = 'Bring the compass to King Anduin Wrynn in Stormwind Keep.', `QuestDescription` = '<The trinket\'s fine brass exterior is inlaid with intricate filigree, though much of the detail has been battered by rocks and waves. Clearing away the grime and salt encrusting the clasp, you manage to open it.\n\nIt is a compass--or was, at least. The glass face is shattered, the needle bent, unmoving.\n\nSet into the lid is a portrait. The paint is faded and waterlogged, but the subject is unmistakable: the face of a young Anduin Wrynn.>', `QuestCompletionLog` = 'Bring the compass to King Anduin Wrynn in Stormwind Keep.' WHERE `ID` = 46268;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'reuse me' WHERE `ID` = 46270;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Summons to the Keep', `LogDescription` = 'Meet with Genn Greymane at Stormwind Keep.', `QuestDescription` = 'Greetings, $n.\n\nYour presence has been requested in the royal court. The crown has urgent need of you!\n\nPlease return to Stormwind at your earliest convenience.\n\nKing Greymane is anticipating your swift arrival.', `QuestCompletionLog` = 'Meet with Genn Greymane at Stormwind Keep.' WHERE `ID` = 46272;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Giver of Quests', `LogDescription` = 'asdf', `QuestDescription` = 'asdf', `QuestCompletionLog` = 'asdf' WHERE `ID` = 46273;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Consoling the King', `LogDescription` = 'Look for King Anduin Wrynn inside Stormwind Cathedral.', `QuestDescription` = 'Anduin hasn\'t been the same since you brought him his father\'s compass. He has become listless... distracted.\n\nWe attempted to console him, to no avail. Yesterday morning, he left the keep without so much as a word.\n\nI ordered the guards to follow him, of course. He went to pray at the cathedral, where he\'s remained ever since.\n\nYou brought this melancholy upon him! You must convince the boy to resume his duties. There\'s a war to be won!' WHERE `ID` = 46274;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'A Kingdom\'s Heart', `LogDescription` = 'Accompany King Anduin on his walk through Stormwind.', `QuestDescription` = 'My father was a legend. He oversaw the rebuilding of Stormwind, stood toe-to-toe with dragons, led the Alliance to numerous victories.\n\nThen, one day, he was just... gone.\n\nI wear his crown, I hold his title. But I\'ve done nothing to earn them... or the faith of my people.\n\nI\'ve spent the war sequestered in the keep, surrounded by guards and advisors. I need to walk the streets of Stormwind, to know whether it is hope or fear that beats in the hearts of my people.\n\nI welcome your company.' WHERE `ID` = 46275;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Contribute to Mage Tower' WHERE `ID` = 46277;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Return to Sender', `LogDescription` = 'Return $1oa Rejected Letters.', `QuestDescription` = 'You\'ve arrived just in time!$B$BUnlike the mail as of late, I\'m afraid.$B$BWe are severely understaffed, and demand is at an all-time high. We simply can\'t keep up!$B$BI\'d love to chat, but I need help catching up before I can rest for even a moment.$B$BFirst thing\'s first. Several parcels of rejected mail have broken loose again; will you help me round them all up and return them to their senders?' WHERE `ID` = 46278;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Zargrom' WHERE `ID` = 46279;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The King\'s Path', `LogDescription` = 'Accompany King Anduin to the Tomb of Sargeras.', `QuestDescription` = 'Now that I have seen the Broken Shore and the terror of the Burning Legion first hand, my eyes have been opened to the truth.\n\nI speak not of the unfathomable evil of the enemy, but of the bravery and sacrifice that such evil brings about in the hearts of our people.\n\nMy father once told me that every king must carry the weight of his own crown. Mine has never felt heavier than it does at this very moment...\n\nPlease take me to the place where my father died, so that I may honor his sacrifice.', `QuestCompletionLog` = 'Accompany King Anduin to the Tomb of Sargeras.' WHERE `ID` = 46282;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '7.2 Broken Shore - Buildings - Mage Tower - Personal Reward Received' WHERE `ID` = 46283;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Legionfall Supplies', `LogDescription` = 'Complete World Quests or slay Rare Elites on the Broken Shore to earn Legionfall War Supplies.', `QuestDescription` = 'If we don\'t build up some respectable fortifications, we\'ll lose our foothold on the Broken Shore.\n\nThat ain\'t gonna happen on my watch, mate!\n\nWe started construction on three key structures: the Mage Tower, the Nether Disruptor, and the Command Center. Each will play a key role in helping us pound the tar out of the Burning Legion.\n\nTo make progress, we need Legionfall War Supplies... and I mean lots of \'em! You bring \'em to me, and I\'ll handle distribution. Got it?' WHERE `ID` = 46286;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Everyone to the Front' WHERE `ID` = 46288;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Return of the Archmage', `LogDescription` = 'Speak to Meryl in the Hall of the Guardian.', `QuestDescription` = 'With Dalaran protected once again, we can all breathe a little easier. \n\nIt is time for us to return to the Hall of the Guardian. I\'m sure Meryl is anxiously awaiting word of our success.' WHERE `ID` = 46290;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Deadmines Strike Back', `LogDescription` = 'Defeat Cookies\' Leftovers in the Deadmines.', `QuestDescription` = 'Breanni sent you? For her, info is always free. Just don\'t call me a snitch.\n\nI\'ve been hangin\' around the Deadmines for years. For the most part, it\'s a pretty easy livin\'. But a few days ago, I started hearing noises of all sorts comin\' from the mines. If you want to get in unnoticed, I\'ll grab us a mine cart and we can get most of the way down without so much as an awkward glace in our direction.\n\nJust let me know when you\'re ready to head in.' WHERE `ID` = 46291;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Pet Battle Challenge: Deadmines', `LogDescription` = 'Defeat Cookies\' Leftovers in the Deadmines.', `QuestDescription` = 'The Deadmines could still use some cleaning up, seems you didn\'t clear the place out last time.\n\nWe\'ll use the ol\' mine cart trick again. Cept, we\'re going to put some flair into it. How do you feel about fire? No? Okay, fine. Just let me know when you\'re ready.' WHERE `ID` = 46292;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Deadmines, Part Three?', `LogDescription` = 'Find Marcus "Bagman" Brown outside the Deadmines in Westfall.', `QuestDescription` = 'I\'ve heard suspicious rumors of movement in the Deadmines. After everything you pulled off in the Wailing Caverns, you\'d be the perfect person to look into this!\n\nI have a friend in Westfall. He may not look like much, but he\'s quick as a whip and may have more information on what is happening in Westfall. We\'ve already dealt with the Van Cleefs... twice. So what could be making that sort of ruckus down there?' WHERE `ID` = 46293;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Overwhelming Power', `LogDescription` = 'Kill $4oa demons.', `QuestDescription` = 'We will find no sanctuary on this world. Even now the full might of the Burning Legion rises to defend Argus.$B$BThe siege camp below overflows with demon filth that stand between us and the weapon trained on the Vindicaar.$B$BThey must be dealt with before it can fully charge, or Argus will be our grave.', `QuestCompletionLog` = 'Meet Illidan Stormrage at the Crown of Destruction.' WHERE `ID` = 46297;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Rare Elite 15' WHERE `ID` = 46304;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Thorim\'s Flame', `LogDescription` = 'Convince the Drekirjar Shrine-Keeper to let you take Thorim\'s Flame.', `QuestDescription` = 'Not too long ago, the Drekirjar and the Thorignir respected each other. This only changed when Skovald came into power. An ancient Drekirjar spirit watches over this peak, which seems to be a sacred graveyard of some sort. He is the keeper of the ceremonial flame, which happens to be exactly what we need to call down the broodmother.$b$bWhy don\'t we go convince him to let us take the flame? I\'m sure he\'ll be nothing but... amiable.' WHERE `ID` = 46305;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Leave a Trail' WHERE `ID` = 46308;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Rare Elite 16' WHERE `ID` = 46313;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Vengeance: Seeking Kor\'vas', `LogDescription` = 'Find Kor\'vas Bloodthorn in the streets of Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'Thankfully, we are not quite alone in uncovering the Legion\'s plots to infiltrate the city.$B$BOne of your Illidari, Kor\'vas Bloodthorn, has taken to patrolling the city streets on her own to find the source behind the recent attacks.$B$BI do not entirely trust your kind, but I will concede that you have at least proved adept at your namesake. I suggest you find Kor\'vas and see what she has uncovered before the Legion strikes once more.\n\n|cFF660000Specialization: Vengeance Demon Hunter|r' WHERE `ID` = 46314;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Prideful Gladiator\'s Leather Armor' WHERE `ID` = 46315;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Champion: Kanrethad Ebonlocke' WHERE `ID` = 46316;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Talon\'s Call', `LogDescription` = 'Speak with Thisalee Crow in the Dreamgrove.', `QuestDescription` = 'The Legion is launching a renewed assault against the Shrine of Aviana in Hyjal!\n\nThisalee Crow is organizing a counter-offensive, she requests your presence in the Dreamgrove at once.\n\nWe will handle the offensive here. Good luck, Archdruid!' WHERE `ID` = 46317;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Defense of Aviana', `LogDescription` = 'Assist Thisalee in the defense of the Shrine of Aviana in Hyjal, then return to her in the Dreamgrove.', `QuestDescription` = 'The situation is dire. The Legion is attacking the Shrine of Aviana in Hyjal, AGAIN! They must be after something specific, but I\'m not sure what.\n\nUs Druids of the Talon are skilled scouts and infiltrators, but are lacking in... durability. They won\'t be able to hold out for long! We must go to help!' WHERE `ID` = 46318;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'You Can\'t Take the Sky from Me', `LogDescription` = 'Deal with Infazzar the Shade, and retrieve the Idol of Aviana.', `QuestDescription` = 'The Shrine of Aviana has fallen to the demons, and the Idol of Aviana has been stolen.\n\nThat idol acts as a link between the Druids of the Talon and the powers of flight granted to us by Aviana.\n\nThe Druids of the Talon have decided to rebuild a new shrine in a more secure location: here in the Dreamgrove.\n\nMeanwhile, I\'m going to get our idol back. Meet me in Azsuna, near where we\'ve tracked Infazzar to, if you want to help.' WHERE `ID` = 46319;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Hope For a Cure', `LogDescription` = 'Return to the Spirit of Brewmaster Blanche in the Temple of Five Dawns.', `QuestDescription` = 'Hopefully you found enough fel poison samples with which to brew a cure.\n\nLet\'s meet back to the Temple of Five Dawns!' WHERE `ID` = 46320;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Krasus\' Landing Searched' WHERE `ID` = 46321;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Pirate\'s Bay', `LogDescription` = 'Meet up with Lilian Voss and Tethys at Dead Man\'s Bay in Azsuna.', `QuestDescription` = 'While we\'ve made some progress on the Broken Shore, I think it is time for the more subtle tactics of the Uncrowned.$b$bWe\'ve received word of a large cave off the main island, where powerful demons meet to plot our downfall. One of our rogues, Lilian Voss, has formulated a plan with Tethys to take care of them, but they require your aid. They are waiting for you at Dead Man\'s Bay in Azsuna.' WHERE `ID` = 46322;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'What\'s the Cache?', `LogDescription` = 'Kill Master Gunner Prix and obtain the Fel-Infused Gunpowder Cache.', `QuestDescription` = 'Our goal is to retrieve a cache of gunpowder which has been infused with some sort of fel power. I don\'t know how the pirates here acquired it, but it is more dangerous than they know. I assure you that it will be more... effective in our hands.$b$bMaster Gunner Prix should be toward the back of the cove, near the water. Take what we need from her.' WHERE `ID` = 46323;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'False Orders', `LogDescription` = 'Plant the False Orders in the marked locations.', `QuestDescription` = 'We must take some precautions. As soon as you assassinate the gunner, the crew will be looking for you. I had Tethys forge some orders in her handwriting that should buy us some time.$b$bPlant the orders in the marked locations. That will take care of the danger.' WHERE `ID` = 46324;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The United Front' WHERE `ID` = 46325;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Jorach\'s Calling', `LogDescription` = 'Return to Lord Jorach Ravenholdt in the Hall of Shadows.', `QuestDescription` = 'And with that, the first phase of my machination is complete. Let\'s return to Jorach and tell him it is time to continue.' WHERE `ID` = 46326;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Bargaining with Shadows', `LogDescription` = 'Meet Ritssyn Flamescowl in the Chamber of the Guardian beneath Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'From the clues you\'ve been able to piece together, it appears that Levia was looking to conduct a ritual in the libraries beneath Dalaran - most likely to summon this "Agatha" she has become so infatuated with. I\'m afraid this is a little out of my area of expertise, so I\'m going to have to call in a favor.\n\nI\'ll send for assistance from the Council of the Black Harvest. One of their warlocks will meet you in the Chamber of the Guardian to assist with your investigation.\n\nI hope we\'re not too late.' WHERE `ID` = 46327;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tracking Quest' WHERE `ID` = 46328;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tracking Quest' WHERE `ID` = 46329;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tracking Quest' WHERE `ID` = 46330;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Tracking Quest' WHERE `ID` = 46331;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = '[DNT]Shadow Priests - Elune Death Enabled' WHERE `ID` = 46332;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Livin\' on the Ledge', `LogDescription` = 'Return to the Fel Hammer and speak with Matron Mother Malevolence.', `QuestDescription` = 'Slayer $p, Matron Mother Malevolence requests an audience with you back at the Fel Hammer. Please see her at your earliest convenience.' WHERE `ID` = 46333;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'To Fel and Back', `LogDescription` = 'Speak with Kyra Lightblade to secure a ride to Felwing Ledge. Then complete the Felwing Ledge scenario.', `QuestDescription` = 'Mardum has its fair share of secrets, one of which we found not too long after we took control of the Fel Hammer. It\'s a breeding ground of sorts, festering with fel bats.$b$bWe\'ve been capturing the pups and trying to train them up for our efforts against the Legion.$b$bBut the other day, we caught an even greater prize, something worthy of your position, Slayer.$b$bSpeak with Kyra and she\'ll provide you a ride to the ledge.' WHERE `ID` = 46334;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Vault of the Tirisgarde', `LogDescription` = 'Find 5 Ancient Artifacts within the Hall of the Guardian.', `QuestDescription` = 'Dalaran\'s weapons are arcane in origin, but that doesn\'t mean we can\'t try something different. \n\nOur order\'s vaults contain a vast store of magical devices... Why don\'t you take a look around and see if there\'s anything we can use?' WHERE `ID` = 46335;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'A Golden Ticket', `LogDescription` = 'Read the Golden Letter in Trueshot Lodge.', `QuestDescription` = 'Huntmaster, we\'ve gotten word from the Lodge that there is a letter wrought from golden light sitting on one of the tables, and it\'s got your name on it.\n\nNo one is sure how it got there, and someone\'s wolf may have tried to open it and gotten a mouth full of singed fur. Seems like it\'s meant only for you.\n\nWe\'ll hold down the fort here while you investigate.' WHERE `ID` = 46336;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Night of the Wilds', `LogDescription` = 'Ask the Herald of Odyn to take you to the Fields of the Eternal Hunt.', `QuestDescription` = '<The letter is written in a flowing, golden script. You can practically hear Odyn\'s booming voice speak the words as you read it.>\n\nThe Night of the Wilds is upon us. \n\nTonight, we will feast in honor of the beasts of legend, and they will rise once more in the Fields of the Eternal Hunt.\n\nOne among us will set out into the fields to put their spirits to rest once more. \n\nMy herald awaits you, hunter, if you will join us.' WHERE `ID` = 46337;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'A Creative Solution', `LogDescription` = 'Talk to Ari.', `QuestDescription` = 'The Nightborne Soulstone may be our best hope if we can come up with a way to safely use it without Kathra\'natir escaping. If he were to get loose in Dalaran...\n\nWe should consult with our friend, Ari. She will know what modifications need to be done.' WHERE `ID` = 46338;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Keymaster Orlis', `LogDescription` = 'Kill Keymaster Orlis and search his body.', `QuestDescription` = 'The Felborne insurgents appear to be guarding a teleporter pad within the glade ahead. I wonder where it leads?\n\nIt is probably safe to assume that we\'ll need to kill Keymaster Orlis in order to gain access.' WHERE `ID` = 46339;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Gates Are Closed', `LogDescription` = 'Return to Archmage Khadgar at the Violet Citadel in Dalaran.', `QuestDescription` = 'Sigryn must be reached before she can confront Odyn, but our path is blocked. Odyn will close the Gates of Valor as soon as he becomes aware of Sigryn\'s assault. You will have to find another way into the Halls.\n\nI have no talent with portals, but your friends at the Kirin Tor seem to be very adept. Go now to them, and find a way though.\n\nI thank you for what you\'ve done to help Sigryn this far, $c. I only hope we can save her from herself.' WHERE `ID` = 46340;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Tale of Ban-Lu', `LogDescription` = 'Listen to Master Bu\'s story.', `QuestDescription` = 'Oh, hello, you must be the new Grandmaster.\n\n<Master Bu squints at you and sniffs.>\n\nYou young ones have no patience these days, always running off to fight your great battles.\n\nNo time for stories, even good ones, eh?\n\nWhy don\'t you put your fists down for a moment and allow an old man to tell you a tale.\n\nMaybe buy an old man a drink while you are at it?' WHERE `ID` = 46341;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Return to the Broken Peak', `LogDescription` = 'Meet Master Bu at the Peak of Serenity.', `QuestDescription` = 'Of course, this is no mere story. Ban-Lu served as the personal mount of each of the previous Grandmasters, accompanying them through their travels as a faithful and trusted companion.\n\nBut... he has not revealed himself since you have become Grandmaster. This is troubling.\n\nThe last time he was seen was at the Peak of Serenity, after the fall of Grandmaster Hight.\n\nIt is there that we must begin our search for him.' WHERE `ID` = 46342;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Trail of Ban-Lu', `LogDescription` = 'Follow the trail of Ban-Lu.', `QuestDescription` = 'It seems a lifetime ago that Grandmaster Hight was walking these grounds. \n\nWhile Ban-Lu has served every previous Grandmaster, he and Hight were the greatest of friends.\n\nFor many years they traveled the land, connecting with its people and maintaining our fragile peace.\n\nI cannot imagine how deeply Ban-Lu must have been affected by his passing.\n\nThere must be some clues to his whereabouts around here. Look sharply.' WHERE `ID` = 46343;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Smelly\'s Luckydo', `LogDescription` = 'Collect 3 parts of Smelly\'s Luckydo.', `QuestDescription` = 'You! Please help! Stupid hozen stole Smelly\'s luckydo! \n\nNow, Smelly always unlucky. Just turned around and look, pack is on fire.\n\nNot going to put fire out because then something ELSE unlucky happen. Maybe something worse!\n\nYou beat up hozen, yes? Get back luckydo? Smelly will help you, any way he can!' WHERE `ID` = 46344;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Into the Hornet\'s Nest', `LogDescription` = 'Use the teleporter pad.', `QuestDescription` = 'I hope you are up for an adventure. Shall we see where that teleporter goes?' WHERE `ID` = 46345;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Shadow of Ban-Lu', `LogDescription` = 'Meet Master Bu at the Shado-Pan Monastery.', `QuestDescription` = 'That was good of you to assist Smelly Mountaintop, Grandmaster, and we have learned more about the fate of Ban-lu.\n\nI won\'t bother you with escorting me to Shado-Pan Monastery. I can manage on my own.\n\nMeet me there and we\'ll continue our search.' WHERE `ID` = 46346;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Clean-up on Aisle Sha', `LogDescription` = 'Help Commander Shen-Li with the remaining Sha.', `QuestDescription` = 'I\'ve spoken with the Shado-pan and they are willing to give us information if we can assist them with a task of their own.\n\nSpeak with Commander Shen-Li. While you\'re assisting them, I shall continue to meditate.' WHERE `ID` = 46347;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The River to Ban-Lu', `LogDescription` = 'Meet with Waterspeaker Ryuli to the southeast.', `QuestDescription` = 'We still do not know where Ban-Lu has gone to, but I do know who might.\n\nTo the southeast lives a jinyu, Waterspeaker Ryuli.\n\nPerhaps he has seen Ban-Lu, or can ask him to inquire with the river about where Ban-Lu has been seen recently?\n\nAll this travel has done a number on my old joints, Grandmaster. I shall rest here a bit longer, and then catch up with you later on.' WHERE `ID` = 46348;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Lilies for Ryuli', `LogDescription` = 'Collect $1oa Moon Lilies for Waterspeaker Ryuli.', `QuestDescription` = 'I have not seen Ban-Lu, but the waters will surely know where he is.\n\nThere is a flower that grows in the lakes of the mountain slopes near the Temple of the White Tiger, that only blooms in the presence of someone pure of heart.\n\nBring me six of these Moon Lilies and I shall use them to speak to the river.' WHERE `ID` = 46349;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'The Trial of Ban-Lu', `LogDescription` = 'Find Ban-Lu at the bottom of the waterfall.', `QuestDescription` = 'Ah, the ripples I feel in the water are strong! The droplet does not fall far from our location.\n\nBan-Lu is quite close. \n\n<Ryuli closes his eyes and releases the lilies into the water. They drift slowly to the east.>\n\nHe waits for you now, at the bottom of the waterfall to the east.', `QuestCompletionLog` = 'Return to Ban-Lu at the Shrine of Inner-Light on the Wandering Isle.' WHERE `ID` = 46350;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Keep it Secret, Keep it Safe', `LogDescription` = 'Return to Ari in the Hall of the Guardian.', `QuestDescription` = 'The shield generator you found is much more than it appears. I do not think my elders would approve of such advanced technology being shared with outlanders...\n\nAnd yet... We owe you our lives and our freedom. \n\nYou may use it, with my blessing. Just... please be discreet about its existence, Archmage $n.' WHERE `ID` = 46351;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Vindictive Combatant\'s MailArmor' WHERE `ID` = 46352;
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogTitle` = 'Master Who?', `LogDescription` = 'Meet Master Bu at Morning Breeze Village outside Temple of the Five Dawns.', `QuestDescription` = 'Greetings. I\'ve just received word that Master Bu has returned from a long spirit journey, and is currently resting his feet at Morning Breeze Village outside of the Temple of Five Dawns.\n\nIt\'s been quite a long time since anyone has seen or heard from him, but he\'s asking to speak to you.\n\nWe will handle the situation here while you are absent, Grandmaster.' WHERE `ID` = 46353;
